不过，对，这里面有一种很好的、共同的仪式感。

1221
00:52:28.960 --> 00:52:31.580
And, I mean, and that's, that's what it was like making the show.
我的意思是，制作这部剧的时候就是这样的。

1222
00:52:31.740 --> 00:52:36.460
We were, we were all going through life together in this way and going through the seasons together.
我们当时就是这样一起经历生活，一起度过每一个季节的。

1223
00:52:36.960 --> 00:52:47.380
And this, this rollercoaster ride of this nine episodes after the strike was, if we weren't, like, bonded together, but before then, which we were.
罢工结束后这九集的过山车般的旅程，即使我们没有紧密相连——其实之前就已经紧密相连了。

1224
00:52:47.380 --> 00:52:55.140
This really, and this was such proof, Pam, of how locked in your stage 22 on the Fox slot was.
帕姆，这真的是最好的证明，证明你们在福克斯第22号摄影棚是多么默契。

1225
00:52:55.600 --> 00:52:56.020
I agree.
我同意。

1226
00:52:56.140 --> 00:53:01.100
With the crew and everybody in there, everybody in post, the production team, the crew, this, like, everybody.
和剧组以及那里的每个人，后期制作的每个人，制片团队，工作人员，就像所有人一样。

1227
00:53:01.800 --> 00:53:08.740
God, what had to happen to do those nine episodes was, I don't think people, it's hard to explain it to the people who weren't there.
天哪，为了拍完那九集所经历的一切，我觉得没经历过的人很难理解。

1228
00:53:08.840 --> 00:53:11.600
And all of those people couldn't wait for season four.
而所有那些人都在迫不及待地等待第四季。

1229
00:53:12.120 --> 00:53:16.420
Yeah, we scared away zero people with every crazy thing we asked them to figure out.
是的，无论我们提出多么疯狂的要求让他们去解决，我们都没有吓退任何人。

1230
00:53:16.420 --> 00:53:17.860
But it was more like, no, I'm here, give me more.
相反，大家的态度是，不，我在这儿，再多给我点。

1231
00:53:17.860 --> 00:53:18.940
Just make them want to come back more.
只会让他们更想看接下来的内容。

1232
00:53:19.320 --> 00:53:21.660
So few people got let go on How I Met Your Mother.
在《老爸老妈浪漫史》剧组，极少有人被解雇。

1233
00:53:21.920 --> 00:53:25.700
If you left How I Met Your Mother, it was because you were retiring from the business.
如果你离开了《老爸老妈浪漫史》，那一定是因为你退休了。

1234
00:53:25.880 --> 00:53:29.420
You were like, it was, you were like, I would like to spend time with my grandkids.
你会说，就像是，我想花时间陪陪我的孙子孙女。

1235
00:53:29.560 --> 00:53:32.020
Like, you know, like, absolutely.
你知道的，就是这样，绝对是的。

1236
00:53:32.400 --> 00:53:33.580
Almost, almost nobody.
几乎，几乎没有别人。

1237
00:53:34.540 --> 00:53:36.560
Yeah, we were really, really lucky.
是的，我们真的非常非常幸运。

1238
00:53:36.720 --> 00:53:38.640
I remember Peter, Peter left camera.
我记得彼得，彼得离开摄影机了。

1239
00:53:39.100 --> 00:53:42.020
I forget what Peter, I loved Peter, he was a lovely guy.
我忘了彼得是……我喜欢彼得，他是个可爱的人。

1240
00:53:42.400 --> 00:53:43.660
Yeah, he retired.
对，他退休了。

1241
00:53:44.700 --> 00:53:46.220
Yeah, so many amazing people.
是啊，有那么多优秀的人。

1242
00:53:46.420 --> 00:53:48.380
Pammy, that's, you bring that out of people.
帕米，那是，你把那种特质从人们身上激发出来了。

1243
00:53:48.640 --> 00:53:49.800
You bring the best out of people.
你激发了人们最好的一面。

1244
00:53:49.980 --> 00:53:50.700
I don't know.
我不知道。

1245
00:53:51.320 --> 00:53:52.280
I can't be overstated.
这怎么强调都不为过。

1246
00:53:52.360 --> 00:53:52.620
I'm so lucky.
我太幸运了。

1247
00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:59.140
We had, Pam, we read a letter in the last episode where the letter writer said,
帕姆，我们在上一集里读了一封信，写信的人说，

1248
00:53:59.260 --> 00:54:04.660
it's the only show I know where the crew is famous to now because of how much we talk about the crew.
这是我唯一知道的一部剧，因为我们经常谈论剧组，导致剧组人员现在都出名了。

1249
00:54:05.500 --> 00:54:06.640
How great is that?
这多棒啊？

1250
00:54:07.040 --> 00:54:07.380
Yeah.
对。

1251
00:54:07.380 --> 00:54:13.920
That's, well, you know, you see, the thing, the thing I think people don't understand is like, you might skip the credits,
那个，就是，你知道的，你看，情况是这样的，我觉得人们不理解的地方在于，比如，你可能会跳过片尾字幕，

1252
00:54:13.920 --> 00:54:20.620
you might stay because you like the song and talk to your friend afterwards and, or, or they, even on Netflix, it drives me crazy.
你可能会因为喜欢这首歌而留下来，之后跟朋友聊天，或者，或者他们，甚至在Netflix上，这也让我抓狂。

1253
00:54:20.620 --> 00:54:21.300
It goes so faSt.
它变得太快了。

1254
00:54:21.740 --> 00:54:23.020
Well, they'll minimize the box.
好吧，他们会把窗口缩小。

1255
00:54:23.120 --> 00:54:23.360
Yeah.
对。

1256
00:54:23.580 --> 00:54:23.880
I hate that.
我讨厌那样。

1257
00:54:23.880 --> 00:54:25.800
And they'll just, I hate that so much.
他们就会，我太讨厌那样了。

1258
00:54:25.900 --> 00:54:26.280
It's terrible.
这太糟糕了。

1259
00:54:26.280 --> 00:54:27.440
I can't tell you how much I hate that.
我简直无法形容我有多讨厌那样。

1260
00:54:27.440 --> 00:54:38.000
But when you are on a TV series and a long running TV series, or you do a movie that's shooting for a long time, the crew is like, they're your people.
但当你参演一部电视剧，一部长期播出的电视剧，或者你拍一部拍摄时间很长的电影时，剧组就像是，他们就是你的人。

1261
00:54:38.220 --> 00:54:41.920
They're the people you're in the trenches with and you adore them.
他们是跟你并肩作战的人，你爱死他们了。

1262
00:54:42.060 --> 00:54:50.260
And so when that name floats by, it's just a, it's just a name to the person sitting in, and they shouldn't feel the same affection, obviously.
所以当那个名字飘过时，对坐在屏幕前的人来说，它只是个名字，而且显然他们不应该怀有同样的喜爱之情。

1263
00:54:50.380 --> 00:54:57.420
They're not going to, but it is an honoring of all the people, you know, and when people win awards and they think the crew is a lot of people.
他们不会的，但这是对所有人的致敬，你知道的，当人们获奖时，他们会觉得剧组有很多人。

1264
00:54:57.420 --> 00:54:59.100
Like, it means so much.
比如，这意味着很多。

1265
00:54:59.320 --> 00:55:00.100
It's really meaningful.
这真的很有意义。

1266
00:55:00.300 --> 00:55:09.680
Dude, I don't know if you've ever talked about this before, but every year, one of the cast members did a photo album for everybody and took,
老兄，我不知道你以前有没有谈过这个，但每年，其中一位演员都会为每个人做一个相册，拍了——

1267
00:55:09.900 --> 00:55:16.740
and it wasn't a photo album of all the guest stars, although they were included.
而且这不是一本全是客串明星的相册，虽然他们也被包含在内。

1268
00:55:17.020 --> 00:55:17.860
No, nor of just the main caSt.
不，也不是只有主要演员的。

1269
00:55:18.160 --> 00:55:19.220
Or of the main caSt.
或者是主要演员的。

1270
00:55:19.480 --> 00:55:21.580
It was, it was the crew.
那是，那是剧组的相册。

1271
00:55:21.860 --> 00:55:24.160
It was everybody who showed up every day.
那是每一个每天都到场的人。

1272
00:55:24.600 --> 00:55:27.100
I think we each had to do two of them, obviously.
我想我们显然每个人都得做两本。

1273
00:55:27.100 --> 00:55:29.740
Maybe, I forget who had to do a third one.
也许吧，我忘了是谁还得做第三本。

1274
00:55:30.060 --> 00:55:31.640
I have all of them right there.
我所有的都在那儿呢。

1275
00:55:31.720 --> 00:55:32.680
It had to be Ali Hanigan.
那肯定是艾莉·汉尼根。

1276
00:55:32.820 --> 00:55:34.100
She would have put her hand up to do that.
她肯定会举手要求做这个。

1277
00:55:34.420 --> 00:55:46.680
Well, it was also, it was stressful because you would get, you would get, I was stressed, but you get so many pictures and you have to kind of sift through them.
好吧，这也是，这很有压力，因为你会得到，你会得到，我当时压力很大，但你会得到那么多照片，你得仔细筛选。

1278
00:55:46.820 --> 00:55:50.960
Like, and how many pictures do we pick a put of Mike Tyson with all these different people?
比如，我们得挑多少张迈克·泰森和这些不同的人合影的照片？

1279
00:55:50.960 --> 00:55:53.200
I took about 14,000 pictures.
我拍了大约14,000张照片。

1280
00:55:53.380 --> 00:55:53.840
Like, truly.
真的。

1281
00:55:54.220 --> 00:55:57.940
I have a hard drive because remember, I always had my camera.
我有一个硬盘，因为记住，我总是带着我的相机。

1282
00:55:58.260 --> 00:56:03.640
And so at the end of every season, I would give them to whoever was, whoever was doing it.
所以在每个季度末，我会把它们交给负责制作的人。

1283
00:56:03.960 --> 00:56:05.840
But it was their, their treasures.
但那是他们的，他们的珍宝。

1284
00:56:06.100 --> 00:56:07.320
Documents of pure joy.
纯粹快乐的记录。

1285
00:56:07.600 --> 00:56:09.640
We also made a great children's book about Pam.
我们还做了一本关于帕姆的棒极了的儿童读物。

1286
00:56:09.640 --> 00:56:14.540
Yes, at the very end of the series, there was a Pam Freyman superhero, the incredible Pam Freyman.
是的，在剧集的最后，有一个帕姆·弗雷曼超级英雄，不可思议的帕姆·弗雷曼。

1287
00:56:14.840 --> 00:56:15.640
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

1288
00:56:16.120 --> 00:56:17.060
That's so good.
太棒了。

1289
00:56:17.220 --> 00:56:19.720
We should, we should take pictures of that and put that in the show notes.
我们应该，我们应该把那个拍下来，放到节目简介里。

1290
00:56:20.100 --> 00:56:21.120
Alec, I can do that.
亚历克，我能做到。

1291
00:56:21.120 --> 00:56:29.580
There was also the Pamela was robbed or the book that Kobe was reading in the tub when I lost the Emmy.
还有《帕梅拉被抢劫》或者科比在我失落艾美奖时在浴缸里读的那本书。

1292
00:56:31.660 --> 00:56:33.060
I forgot about that.
我都把这事忘了。

1293
00:56:33.280 --> 00:56:34.360
That's so funny.
太搞笑了吧。

1294
00:56:34.700 --> 00:56:34.820
Yeah.
对。

1295
00:56:35.280 --> 00:56:35.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1296
00:56:35.620 --> 00:56:35.880
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

1297
00:56:36.420 --> 00:56:37.300
Cute people.
真是一群可爱的人。

1298
00:56:37.860 --> 00:56:44.640
To bring it back to the episode from one more saga and before we finish, the one thing we should also talk about is just Barney and Ted's friendship reunion.
为了在结束前再把话题拉回这一集的另一个传奇故事，我们还应该讨论的一件事就是巴尼和泰德的友情重聚。

1299
00:56:44.820 --> 00:56:51.540
The big thing in this back nine episodes, the biggest story of all besides Stella, biggest running story, Marcy Miller having financial probleMs.
最后这九集里的重头戏，除了斯特拉之外最核心的故事，最大的主线故事，玛西·米勒遇到了财务问题。

1300
00:56:51.660 --> 00:56:53.160
There's a bunch of cool, juicy runners.
还有一堆很酷、很带劲的次要剧情线。

1301
00:56:53.440 --> 00:56:56.600
But the biggest one is the bro breakup between Barney and Ted.
但其中最大的一桩，是巴尼和泰德的兄弟决裂。

1302
00:56:56.600 --> 00:56:58.380
And when they reunite,
当他们重聚时，

1303
00:56:58.540 --> 00:57:10.180
when Ted realizes Barney ran miles to be by his bedside and only failed to arrive there because he was crushed by a bus going 40 miles an hour the wrong way on a one-way street,
当泰德意识到巴尼跑了好几英里来到他的病床前，只是因为在单行道上被一辆逆行时速40英里的公交车撞扁了而没能赶到，

1304
00:57:10.840 --> 00:57:13.640
is like, that is such a moving reunion.
就觉得，那真是一场感人的重聚。

1305
00:57:14.040 --> 00:57:14.140
Yeah.
对。

1306
00:57:14.400 --> 00:57:15.860
Like, really, like, heartfelt.
真的，就觉得，很走心。

1307
00:57:16.120 --> 00:57:16.860
It's ridiculous.
太荒谬了。

1308
00:57:16.860 --> 00:57:18.640
He's in, like, the full body cast, Barney.
他当时全身打着石膏，巴尼。

1309
00:57:18.740 --> 00:57:19.320
It's absurd.
这太离谱了。

1310
00:57:19.380 --> 00:57:24.500
But I was choked up watching that reunion because a lot of episodes went by.
但我看那场重聚时还是哽咽了，因为中间隔了很多集。

1311
00:57:24.500 --> 00:57:28.720
One of the great unspoken love stories of How I Met Your Mother is Barney and Ted.
《老爸老妈浪漫史》中伟大的未明言的爱情故事之一，就是巴尼和泰德。

1312
00:57:28.860 --> 00:57:29.260
It is.
确实是。

1313
00:57:29.380 --> 00:57:31.920
It's a turbulent love story, but a love story nonetheless.
这是一个波折的爱情故事，但终究是个爱情故事。

1314
00:57:32.380 --> 00:57:33.800
And it's, they are brothers.
而且，他们是兄弟。

1315
00:57:34.080 --> 00:57:34.820
That's what they say.
他们是这么说的。

1316
00:57:34.900 --> 00:57:35.420
We're brothers.
我们是兄弟。

1317
00:57:35.700 --> 00:57:36.180
And it's true.
事实也确实如此。

1318
00:57:36.380 --> 00:57:40.620
I thought for the comedy, it was great to have him in all that stuff.
从喜剧效果来看，我觉得让他搞成那样挺棒的。

1319
00:57:41.080 --> 00:57:47.080
But the realism of it is, like, I think we cut to, he's fine the next, the beginning of season four.
但现实点说，我觉得我们切过去时，到了第四季初他就没事了。

1320
00:57:47.080 --> 00:57:47.800
Is he paralyzed?
他瘫痪了吗？

1321
00:57:48.040 --> 00:57:49.440
Like, he's really got horribly mangled.
就是，他真的伤得面目全非。

1322
00:57:49.440 --> 00:57:51.480
He looked, like, really horribly mangled.
他看起来，真的伤得面目全非。

1323
00:57:51.520 --> 00:57:52.400
It really looked bad, yeah.
看起来真的很惨，对。

1324
00:57:52.400 --> 00:57:54.420
It really looked horrifyingly bad.
看起来真的惨不忍睹。

1325
00:57:54.520 --> 00:57:56.420
It was like, we over-did everything.
就好像，我们有点用力过猛了。

1326
00:57:56.560 --> 00:57:57.400
Everyone was too old.
每个人都显得太老了。

1327
00:57:57.540 --> 00:57:58.580
Barney was too injured there.
巴尼当时伤得太重了。

1328
00:57:59.820 --> 00:58:04.000
Well, that was the kind of thing, you guys, you rooted it in some real emotional truth.
嗯，这就是那种情况，伙计们，你们把它扎根于某些真实的情感真相中。

1329
00:58:04.040 --> 00:58:07.340
And then you always kind of tipped your hat to the multicam sitcom.
然后你们总会向多机位情景喜剧致敬。

1330
00:58:07.500 --> 00:58:08.660
Like, this is also ridiculous.
比如，这也太荒唐了。

1331
00:58:08.680 --> 00:58:11.060
We're also going to acknowledge the form we're in.
我们也要承认我们所处的表现形式。

1332
00:58:11.320 --> 00:58:12.940
Yeah, I mean, it was true.
对，我的意思是，确实如此。

1333
00:58:12.940 --> 00:58:16.820
And, like, Pam, I keep on saying in this back nine, the other big theme is underthinking.
而且，帕姆，我在这后半季里一直在说，另一个大主题就是不去过度思考。

1334
00:58:17.080 --> 00:58:19.320
We had no time to overthink anything.
我们没有时间去过度思考任何事情。

1335
00:58:19.500 --> 00:58:20.840
It was like, Britney Spears, sure.
就觉得，布兰妮·斯皮尔斯，行啊。

1336
00:58:21.080 --> 00:58:22.820
We'll do Britney, we'll get Britney Spears in here.
我们就拍布兰妮，把布兰妮·斯皮尔斯请到这儿来。

1337
00:58:23.560 --> 00:58:24.580
Barney's hit by a bus.
巴尼被公交车撞了。

1338
00:58:24.700 --> 00:58:26.040
He's in a full body cast, sure.
他全身打着石膏，行啊。

1339
00:58:26.460 --> 00:58:30.420
It's like, no, there just wasn't time to second guess anything.
就好像，不，根本没有时间去质疑任何事情。

1340
00:58:30.560 --> 00:58:31.880
You had to just go by instinct.
你只能凭直觉行事。

1341
00:58:31.880 --> 00:58:33.540
And some of it we've talked about.
其中有些事我们已经讨论过了。

1342
00:58:33.760 --> 00:58:35.800
There's some moments in this back nine that are insane.
这后半季里有些时刻简直疯狂。

1343
00:58:36.660 --> 00:58:40.240
But there's some moments of, like, legitimately, there's lunacy.
但有些时刻，怎么说呢，名副其实，有些是疯狂的。

1344
00:58:40.240 --> 00:58:42.360
And then there's kind of, like, inspired lunacy in here.
然后这里面还有点，怎么说，灵光乍现的疯狂。

1345
00:58:42.500 --> 00:58:47.180
And there's also, like, genuinely moving big swings that are really interesting.
而且还有，那种真正感人的大手笔，非常有趣。

1346
00:58:47.540 --> 00:58:47.680
Always hard.
一直都很难。

1347
00:58:48.100 --> 00:58:48.440
Yeah.
对。

1348
00:58:48.440 --> 00:58:54.160
And I don't know if it would have, it wouldn't have been quite this way if we'd had more time to do it.
而且我不知道它会不会，如果我们有更多时间来做的话，就不会是现在这个样子了。

1349
00:58:54.220 --> 00:58:55.420
It wouldn't have quite been this.
不会完全是这样的。

1350
00:58:55.540 --> 00:58:58.940
I mentioned this, Pam, in episode 19.
帕姆，我在第19集里提到过这个。

1351
00:58:59.680 --> 00:59:04.420
But when episode 20 started, and episode 19 was kind of, you know,
但是当第20集开始时，而第19集有点，你知道的，

1352
00:59:04.480 --> 00:59:06.400
there was a strong A story and a strong B story.
有一条很强的A线剧情和一条很强的B线剧情。

1353
00:59:06.440 --> 00:59:08.680
And there were Ted's red boots, which you knew wasn't my favorite.
还有泰德的红靴子，你知道那可不是我的最爱。

1354
00:59:08.680 --> 00:59:09.740
I was just going to say, there were boots.
我正想说，有靴子。

1355
00:59:09.740 --> 00:59:10.440
There were boots.
有靴子。

1356
